  "notes": "Drawn from XA-VIX (A320neo, stored at Roswell, 2025-12-02, left side from above) and XA-VXJ (A321neo, 2025-10-18, left side from below), sharing the 2024 scheme's measured geometry where the elements match (red fin circle, aft circle). Engines and winglets vary: green (XA-VXJ), red (XA-VIX), or red and green. Introduced in the late 2010s; the year wasn't confirmed. The gray ring spills a little onto the fuselage below the fin root, not drawn. Still on part of the fleet in 2025-2026 as aircraft are repainted. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on XA-VIX itself (A320neo, from above), placed by its doors and overwing exits: 'viva' runs 0.161 to 0.282 and 'aerobus' 0.207 to 0.283 (lowercase 0.71 of its ascenders); 'viva' has no capitals, so its xHeight 0.65 states the measured lowercase against the nominal cap height. The aft and fin circles sit where the 2024 scheme's do on this photo; the circles, ring and dots are now drawn smooth.",
  "history": "Replaced by the October 2024 'viva' scheme (standard), applied as aircraft are repainted."
}
